                          AuditPanelColumn/Row/Display, AuditPanelProjection, AuditPanelDiagnostics, AuditPanelRegistration)
  - AuditPanel.cs        (WinUI 3 view: ContentControl rendering the loading / empty / data web branches)
Tests (required by acceptance + gate): apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/FeatureViews/AuditPanelTests.cs (31 tests)
  + AuditPanel.Model.cs linked into TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj (headless net10.0 adapter/projection verification).

Web source parity (web/src/features/admin/components/dlq-inspector/AuditPanel.tsx):
  States reproduced (exact branch precedence): !loading && rows.length===0 -> EmptyState (scoped vs global copy);
    else the DataTable, whose empty message is loading ? "Loading audit log..." : "No replay attempts yet". The web
    source is presentational (props: rows/loading/scopedDlqId; only useTranslation) so there is no fetch-driven
    error/stale/offline branch to reproduce, exactly as the TelemetryErrorsPanel/ResultPanel ports document.
  Shared components mapped: @/components/ui DataTable -> TsDataTable/TsDataColumn/TsDataRow, Badge -> TsBadge variant
    via DlqReplayResultVariant (the web RESULT_VARIANT record + its `?? neutral` fallback, computed + unit-tested);
    @/components/data-display TimeStamp format="absolute" -> DateTimeFormatting.Format(.., Full, now);
    @/components/feedback EmptyState -> TsEmptyState. The shared TsDataTable renders text cells, so the result column
    shows its replay-result code (the textual content of the web Badge) while the status tint is verified in the projection.
  Columns (7, in order): replayed_at, actor, dlq_id, result, dst_topic, error, trace_id. Cell renders mirror the web:
    absolute timestamp, x || em-dash fallbacks, numeric dlq_id, raw result code. Pagination defaultPageSize=25.
  i18n: every label resolves through the P1/S10 ILocalizer facade using the SAME catalog keys the web source feeds
    into t(): translation.admin.dlq.audit.cols.{replayedAt,actor,dlqId,result,dstTopic,error,traceId},
    .empty.{title,scopedMessage,globalMessage}, .loading (+ .panels.audit for the data-state region name). All present
    in Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw; no English literals in native code.
  Accessibility: Narrator name on every state (loading text / title+message / audit-log label); the loading table is a
    polite live region; TsDataTable exposes DataGrid semantics and conveys each row through its cell values.
  Telemetry: AuditPanelDiagnostics emits "view.opened slug=AuditPanel" (PII-safe; never actor/dlq_id/trace_id/error)
    on first load.

Pre-existing build-unblock (NOT introduced by this surface):
  The integration baseline did not load: apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj was malformed in
  THREE places -- the ToolCard/ColorConverter, ByteSizeConverter/HashCalculator and TirePressure/CronParser comment
  blocks had each lost their opening "<!--" (the comment text leaked into the preceding ItemGroup, two of which were
  then left unclosed), producing MSB4025 "ItemGroup start tag does not match end tag of Project". This blocked the whole
  solution build/test for ANY surface on this branch. Minimal, structure-restoring fix: re-added the three missing
  "<!--" openers and the two missing "</ItemGroup>" closers (comment/ItemGroup counts now balance 19/19). No Compile
  items were added, removed or reordered. Verified: 6972 headless tests pass with zero regressions.

